I keep checking back every few months and finding that it's still
3.4.3, sigh. Well at least there's an interesting topic on the
newsgroup. :)

Here's an idea: for the "vs. monster class" weapons, instead of giving
them double damage which is useless against everything else, give them
+d5 to hit against everything, and an additional effect which is
especially useful against the class of monster they are meant to
fight.

Reflection for Dragonbane is a good example. When it strikes a
creature with a breath weapon, it should remove that creature's
resistance against its own breath so that reflection actually helps
kill it. Perhaps it could also remove flying or levitation (minor, but
fun).

Trollsbane could remove regeneration from any monster it hits -- and
grant (hungry) regeneration to the wielder? and be an axe (yeah, less
damage, but better for flavor)?

Werebane could grant unchanging and protection from shapechangers.
Also, it's a silver saber. :)

Giantslayer could be a dwarvish spear (good flavor with dwarves vs.
giants, +2 hit bonus vs. H and others), deal +3d8 damage against large
creatures, provide protection from any stone or glass projectile, and
give the boulder evasion described above.

Ogresmasher could give its enhancement bonus to Strength. If
Trollsbane is an axe, this could be the morningstar.

Sting should be a light source, give real warning, cut webs, and deal
x2 damage vs. s,x,c.

Orcrist giving PR is good. Keep the x2 damage vs. orcs (but +d5 hit
against all, as described above). Sting's orc-only warning could be
moved here so the code isn't wasted.

Grimtooth doing poison is not too shabby. Should also confer PR.

Demonbane is a tough one, especially considering how good Grayswandir
is. For starters, this should probably be a silver weapon, but there
are already two sabers, I want Giantslayer to be a spear (not silver,
but the class is represented), and daggers are weeeeak. But maybe with
the right abilities... okay, silver dagger. Stealing from the
Silverfang suggestion, it should engrave like an athame. It should
prevent teleportation into or out of a radius around the wielder, and
prevent any sort of summoning within the same radius. And how's this:
it drains levels from any drain-resistant creature (except riders?),
but not from others.

Firebrand... hmm. :)  You know, I don't even remember whether it's a
lightsource, but it should be. Maybe it could burn any creature
striking you, as if you were a fire elemental?

